<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>SPIKE: shared vs M365-group mailbox Graph subscription + Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` model; size the `GraphSubscriptionManager` + permission-grant delta (FR-15 sizing) — WRITTEN FINDING ONLY</title>
    <phase>P5 — FR-15 capture (parallel, spike-first)</phase>
    <gate>none</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>investigation, spike</tags>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Investigation/spike — the deliverable is a WRITTEN FINDING (notes/) that sizes the shared-vs-group mailbox subscription/permission model + the `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta; it changes no product code, so FULL implementation gates do not apply. It carries an escalation trigger: if the shared-vs-group subscription/permission model requires a design decision beyond sizing, the spike STOPS and surfaces it. 051 is gated on this finding.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Sizing an unfamiliar Microsoft-platform boundary (Graph change-notifications over shared vs M365-group mailboxes + Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` scoping) where getting the permission/subscription model right determines whether 051 is safe to build; reasoning + platform-knowledge synthesis, not code.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Read-only investigation on the independent FR-15 capture track — fully parallel to P1–P4; writes only a finding under notes/; no shared code touched.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies></dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Run the **FR-15 capture spike**. Produce a **written finding** (a notes/ document) that sizes how to extend capture (Graph change-notification subscriptions + Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy`) to cover **shared mailboxes** and **M365 group mailboxes**, and specifies the concrete **`GraphSubscriptionManager` delta** + the **permission-grant delta** needed. **This spike writes NO product code** — its output is the finding that gates 051.

    Investigate + document:
    1. **Subscription model** — how a Graph change-notification subscription differs (if at all) for a shared mailbox vs an M365 group mailbox vs a user mailbox: resource path, supported change types, subscription lifetime/renewal, and any per-mailbox-type limitations.
    2. **Permission model** — the app-only permission surface for reading shared + group mailbox messages, and how **Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy`** scopes app-only access to specific mailboxes (the least-privilege posture; how a policy is created + which app + which mailbox group).
    3. **`GraphSubscriptionManager` delta** — the concrete, minimal change to the existing `Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` to add shared/group coverage (what enumerates the mailboxes, what creates/renews the subscriptions, what changes in the notification handling).
    4. **Sizing + risks** — effort, sequencing, and the risk items 051 must handle (e.g. renewal cadence, group-vs-shared divergence, tenant permission-grant prerequisites the operator must perform).

    Consult the researcher subagent / `knowledge/` for current Microsoft-platform behavior (Graph + Exchange are rapidly-evolving; verify against current docs, not stale memory). If, during investigation, the shared-vs-group subscription/permission model requires a **design decision beyond sizing** (e.g. the two mailbox types need fundamentally different capture paths, or the least-privilege posture forces an architectural choice), **STOP and surface it** — do not pre-decide it inside the spike.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke platform investigator for the communication capture layer. Fluent in the existing `GraphSubscriptionManager` capture path, Microsoft Graph change-notification subscriptions, Exchange Online `ApplicationAccessPolicy` least-privilege scoping, and ADR-028 app-only background auth. Uses the researcher subagent + `knowledge/` for current Microsoft-platform behavior. Produces a written finding; changes no product code.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A written finding at `projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/` that: (a) states the subscription model for shared vs M365-group vs user mailboxes; (b) states the app-only permission model + the Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` least-privilege posture; (c) specifies the concrete minimal `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta + the permission-grant delta; (d) sizes the 051 implementation with sequencing + risks + operator prerequisites. If a design decision beyond sizing surfaces, the finding documents it as an escalation (not a silent decision). 051 is gated on this finding.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-15 extends capture to shared + M365-group mailboxes (D-07). r1 OWNS this — r4 capture is archived with no active owner. The spec mandates spike-first: task 050 confirms the subscription/permission model + the `GraphSubscriptionManager` / permission-grant delta before 051 implements. This track is fully parallel to the intelligence spine (Phases 1–4) — independent.

      The existing capture path is `Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` (user-mailbox subscriptions today). The unknowns the spike resolves: does a shared/group mailbox subscription use the same resource path + change types? What app-only permissions + `ApplicationAccessPolicy` scoping are needed (least privilege)? What is the minimal delta to add the coverage? Graph + Exchange behavior is rapidly-evolving — verify against current docs via the researcher / `knowledge/`.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs (REFERENCE — the existing capture path; the spike specifies the delta, does not edit it)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (app-only background auth — the permission posture the spike sizes against)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/ (OUTPUT — the written finding lands here)</file>
      <file>knowledge/ (consult FIRST for current Microsoft-platform behavior; researcher subagent memoizes findings)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>None — fully parallel/independent capture track.</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-15">Scope: spike-first — confirm the subscription/permission model for shared vs group mailboxes + the `GraphSubscriptionManager` / permission-grant delta; implementation (051) is GATED on this finding. This task produces a WRITTEN FINDING and changes NO product code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: size the shared/group capture against app-only background auth (least privilege); the Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` posture MUST scope app-only access to the intended mailboxes, not tenant-wide.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §15 (researcher)">Scope: Graph + Exchange are rapidly-evolving — consult `knowledge/` FIRST, then current Microsoft Learn / official repos via the researcher subagent; do NOT rely on stale memory for the subscription/permission model.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: no product code change; the deliverable is a notes/ finding. Do NOT begin 051's implementation inside this spike.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/plan.md</file>
