      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` (the current user-mailbox subscription path) + ADR-028 (app-only posture) + the FR-15 spec acceptance criteria.</step>
    <step order="2">Consult `knowledge/` for Graph change-notification + Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` behavior; use the researcher subagent for any current/uncertain platform behavior (subscription resource paths, change types, renewal, per-mailbox-type limits).</step>
    <step order="3">Document the SUBSCRIPTION model: shared vs M365-group vs user mailbox differences (resource path, change types, lifetime/renewal, limitations).</step>
    <step order="4">Document the PERMISSION model: app-only permissions for shared + group mailbox reads + the Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` least-privilege scoping (who grants, which app, which mailboxes) — the operator prerequisites.</step>
    <step order="5">Specify the concrete minimal `GraphSubscriptionManager` DELTA (enumerate mailboxes, create/renew subscriptions, notification-handling changes) + the permission-grant delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Size 051: effort, sequencing, risks (renewal cadence, group-vs-shared divergence, tenant grant prerequisites), and the closed set of behaviors 051 must implement. If a design decision beyond sizing surfaced, document it as an escalation item (do not pre-decide).</step>
    <step order="7">Write the finding to `projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/` (e.g. `notes/050-fr15-mailbox-capture-spike.md`); update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (050 ✅) + `current-task.md`; note whether the escalation trigger fired.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>REQUIRED: if the shared-vs-group mailbox subscription or permission model requires a DECISION BEYOND SIZING — e.g. shared and group mailboxes need fundamentally different capture paths, the least-privilege `ApplicationAccessPolicy` posture forces an architectural choice, or a tenant permission-grant prerequisite changes the ownership/scope of the work — STOP and surface it per root §6 / §6.5. This is a legitimate spike stop; do NOT silently pre-decide the model inside the spike, and do NOT begin 051's implementation to "prove" a decision.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect `GraphSubscriptionManager.cs`, ADR-028, knowledge/, spec FR-15</tool>
    <tool name="researcher">Deep-dive current Graph change-notification + Exchange ApplicationAccessPolicy behavior (Microsoft Learn / official repos)</tool>
    <tool name="write">Author the written finding under notes/</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/050-fr15-mailbox-capture-spike.md (NEW — subscription model + permission model + `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta + permission-grant delta + 051 sizing + risks + any escalation item)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md + current-task.md (UPDATED — 050 ✅; escalation-fired flag noted)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A written finding exists under notes/ stating the Graph subscription model for shared vs M365-group vs user mailboxes (resource path, change types, lifetime/renewal, limitations).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The finding states the app-only permission model + the Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` least-privilege scoping + the operator permission-grant prerequisites.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The finding specifies a concrete, minimal `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta + the permission-grant delta needed for shared/group coverage.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The finding sizes 051 (effort, sequencing, risks, the closed set of behaviors 051 must implement) so 051 can be gated on it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (no code): the spike changes no product code — its only output is the notes/ finding (+ index update).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If a design decision beyond sizing surfaced, it is documented as an escalation item (surfaced per root §6/§6.5), not silently pre-decided.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Escalation trigger is REQUIRED here — a shared-vs-group model decision beyond sizing is a legitimate stop. 051 is GATED on this finding. Fully parallel to the intelligence spine (independent capture track). Consult `knowledge/` + the researcher subagent for current Microsoft-platform behavior — do NOT rely on stale memory. No product code in this task.
  </notes>

